\begin{lemma}\label{lem:martingale_brownian_sq_sub_time}
  \uses{def:brownianNaturalFiltration}
  \lean{ProbabilityTheory.martingale_brownian_sq_sub_time}
The process \(B_t^2-t\) is a martingale with respect to the natural Brownian filtration.
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
It is adapted because \(B_t\) is \(\mathcal F^B_t\)-measurable and \(t\) is
deterministic.  It is integrable because \(B_t\) is Gaussian with finite second
moment.

